{meta: title Long Time Travelin’}
{meta: x_lyrics_source bluegrass-lyrics}
{meta: x_lyrics_url https://www.bluegrasslyrics.com/song/long-time-travelin/}

{start_of_chorus}
Been a long time travelin’ here below
Been a long time travelin’ away from my home
Been a long time travelin’ here below
Gonna lay this ol’ body down
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
When I can read my titles clear
To mansions in the sky
I’ll bid farewell to every fear
And wipe my weepin’ eye
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
May tears like a wild deluge come
And storms of sorrow fall
May I but safely reach my home
My God my heaven my all
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
There I shall bathe my weary soul
In seas of heavenly rest
And not a wave of trouble roll
Across my peaceful breast
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
alternate version:
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Ye fleeting charms of earth farewell
Your springs of joy are dry
My soul now seeks another home
A brighter world on high
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Farewell my friends whose tender care
Has long engaged my love
Your fond embrace I now exchange
For better friends above
{end_of_verse}

